01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
Walk, Don't Run is a 1966 American romantic comedy film directed by Charles Walters (in his final film as a
director), and starring Cary Grant (in his final film role), Samantha Eggar, and Jim Hutton.

11
01:18:22,500 --> 01:18:28,500
It follows a travelling industrialist visiting Tokyo, and accompanying a male
athlete and a female apartment tenant, during the 1964 Summer Olympics.

12
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
The film is a remake of the 1943 film The More the Merrier.

13
01:32:37,500 --> 01:32:43,500
The title stems from the basic rule of racewalking: that competitors
must not run at any point (both feet leaving the ground).

14
01:39:45,000 --> 01:39:51,000
The film explores themes of hotel room, olympic
games, embassy, housing shortage.

15
01:46:52,500 --> 01:46:58,500
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
